; Schema-compile family, 2 of 4. The discriminant IS a closed enum here —
; `kind-tag` admits `kick` and `bass` — and the variant is declared for
; `bogus`, which is neither. The variant could therefore never be selected
; by any document, so the schema is rejected rather than silently carrying a
; branch that is dead by construction.
;
; This is the check `discriminant-not-closed-enum` never reaches: without a
; closed enum there is no membership to test, which is why that case stops
; at one diagnostic instead of also reporting its variant.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name kind-tag
    :underlying symbol
    :members (member-set :values [kick bass]))
  (form :name track
    :discriminant kind
    (key :name kind :type kind-tag :optional true)
    (variant :when bogus
      (key :name step :type number :optional true))))

(track :kind kick)
